    skos:prefLabel 'mole_concentration_of_dissolved_nitrogen_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Mole concentration" means number of moles per unit volume, also called "molarity", and is used in the construction "mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as "nitrogen" or a phrase such as "nox_expressed_as_nitrogen". "Dissolved nitrogen" means the sum of all nitrogen in solution: inorganic nitrogen (nitrite, nitrate and ammonium) plus nitrogen in carbon compounds.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::UAHJU591'^^xsd:string .
